2a) Approved access policy - LIVE SITE AND ALL TRIAL SITES:
        After migrate, and before reloading the web app, use the target site's
        virtual environment and credentials. Preview then apply the reviewed
        permissions/groups with a NEW private backup filename on each run:

        python manage.py sync_access_policy --dry-run
        python manage.py sync_access_policy --apply --backup permissions-before.json
        python manage.py sync_access_policy --dry-run

        Keep the backup outside public/media/static directories. Direct old role
        flags or flags on unrecognised groups require review before application;
        the command will explain these and stop without making changes.
        Third-party permissions and staff/superuser flags remain unchanged.
        Officers also become ExecMembers. Check WebAdmin staff access separately
        for admin-only deletion. Collect static files and reload after applying.
        Full verification and rollback instructions: GarageSale/PERMISSION_DEPLOYMENT.md

2b) Template transfer - LIVE SITE AND ALL TRIAL SITES (new or existing databases):
        Deploy the transfer_templates command before importing. Use the target
        site's project directory, virtual environment and credentials/database.
        On the installation containing the approved current templates, export
        the communication templates and their uploaded attachments to a new
        bundle file. Use development only if its templates are the approved set:

        python manage.py transfer_templates export deployment-templates.json

        Export a fresh bundle for this deployment; the repository's historical
        TemplateData.json fixture is not a substitute. With no --category filter,
        the bundle includes every category and all dated template versions.

        Copy deployment-templates.json to each live/trial server using the
        PythonAnywhere Files app or the normal file-transfer process. After
        migrations, validate and import it on EACH target site:

        python manage.py transfer_templates import deployment-templates.json --dry-run
        python manage.py transfer_templates import deployment-templates.json

        Identical versions are skipped. Conflicting versions stop the import;
        review the differences before explicitly replacing those versions:

        python manage.py transfer_templates import deployment-templates.json --replace --dry-run
        python manage.py transfer_templates import deployment-templates.json --replace

        Use from dates are preserved. Uploaded attachments are included, but
        images/assets linked from template HTML must be accessible separately.
        This is required on the live site as well as the trial sites; it does
        not transfer contributors, event configuration or credentials.
        Full instructions: GarageSale/TEMPLATE_TRANSFER.md

2c) Diary calendar template transfer - SITES WITH DIARY ENABLED:
        Install the approved DjangoTaskCalendar package before this step.
        Apply its migrations with the project's normal migration command.
        Complete the access policy setup in step 2a.
        Check the configured Diary groups:

        python manage.py validate_diary_configuration

        Use transfer_diary_templates to export and import Diary calendar templates.
        This command is separate from the communication template command in step 2b.
        Use the site's project directory, virtual environment, and database credentials.
        Diary 0.1.10.2 treats command-line access as administrative authorization.
        Its transfer command does not accept an --actor argument.
        The current DIARY_MANAGER setting selects the Officer group.

        Export the selected template to a new file on the source site:

        python manage.py transfer_diary_templates export deployment-diary-template.json --template "Garage Sale calendar"

        Replace the template name when the deployment uses a different template.
        Without --template, the export contains every template's latest approved version.
        Export does not overwrite an existing file.
        The file includes milestone declarations, task ownership, date rules, and dependencies.
        Person assignments use email addresses instead of source user IDs.
        The file does not contain event Diaries, task completion records, or user accounts.

        Copy the file to the destination site through the normal file-transfer process.
        Validate the file before import:

        python manage.py transfer_diary_templates import deployment-diary-template.json --dry-run
        python manage.py transfer_diary_templates import deployment-diary-template.json

        Use this command instead of loaddata for Diary template imports.
        The command checks ownership, milestone declarations, and dependency cycles.
        Identical approved versions remain unchanged.
        Conflicting content stops the import.
        Review conflicts before adding --new-version to both import commands.
        Existing milestone labels and descriptions must match the file.
        Add --person-map SOURCE_EMAIL=LOCAL_EMAIL when an assigned person's destination email differs.

        Import the approved template before creating events.
        Its name must match the DIARY_TEMPLATE_NAME setting.
        Event creation supplies dates for the template's required task milestones.
        Existing event Diaries remain unchanged after template import.
        Full integration instructions: GarageSale/DIARY_INTEGRATION.md.
        Package command documentation: Diary/README.md in the DjangoTaskCalendar source repository.

2d) Demonstration data - TRIAL SITES ONLY. DO NOT RUN ON THE LIVE SITE:
        Complete migrations and access policy setup before importing the example Diary template.
        Use the trial site's project directory, virtual environment, and database credentials.
        Import the example calendar template before creating a demonstration event:

        python manage.py transfer_diary_templates import GarageSale/fixtures/diary_demo_template.json --dry-run
        python manage.py transfer_diary_templates import GarageSale/fixtures/diary_demo_template.json

        This example creates the approved template named Garage Sale calendar.
        It contains eight tasks assigned to ExecMember, with booking milestones and task dependencies.
        Set DIARY_TEMPLATE_NAME to Garage Sale calendar for these demonstrations.
        Resolve import conflicts as described in step 2c.
        A new event receives its Diary through the normal event creation service.
        Import alone does not create a Diary for an existing event.
        Use ensure_event_diary(event, user) for existing-event setup as documented in GarageSale/DIARY_INTEGRATION.md.

        After migrations, ensure the trial site's current event is configured:
        its Use from date must be before today and its event date must not have
        passed. Creating a future event does not automatically make it current:
        the current event is the one with the latest Use from date strictly
        before today. A Use from date of today is not eligible until tomorrow.
        For example, to demonstrate the 27 June 2027 event now, edit that event
        and set Use from to yesterday (later than other eligible Use from dates).
        Leave the event date as 27 June 2027.

        From the TRIAL project directory and virtual environment, with
        the TRIAL database credentials, inspect and then build the sample data:

        python manage.py seed_team_demo --dry-run
        python manage.py seed_team_demo

        Creates 8 sponsors with logos (4 contacted, 4 without contact history),
        2 confirmed donors (GBP 250 cash and a GBP 50 gift hamper), and 4 market
        traders (2 invited). All names begin [TEAM DEMO]. No emails are sent.
        Reruns avoid duplicates and preserve changes made during demonstrations;
        they do not reset the data. Ensure trial media files are served so the
        generated logos appear. Transfer templates first for PDF/email demos.
        Full instructions: Contributors/TEAM_DEMO.md

